Noetherian local ring $A$ with finite residue field of characteristic $p$ has
finite image, where $G_{\Q,S}$ denotes the Galois group of the maximal
extension of $\Q$ unramified outside $S$. This proves the two-dimensional odd
case of Boston's strengthening of the unramified Fontaine--Mazur conjecture
