\\
  In this article, we introduce a new rewriting method for computing hom-bases
of diagrammatic categories. Our approach is based on stratified presentations,
obtained by partitioning an equational presentation into strata according to
the rewriting behavior of its relations. We establish modularity principles for
termination and confluence in stratified rewriting systems with coefficients in
a ring. We then introduce a completion procedure that transforms a stratified
presentation into a normalized one, in which mixed interactions between
successive strata are absorbed into the normalized rewriting rules, thereby
inducing modularity of confluence. This leads to a stratified hom-basis theorem
